## Why This Is Asked
This problem tests DP formulation for selecting multiple non-overlapping subarrays with reconstruction—a common pattern in budget allocation and resource optimization scenarios.

## Key Concepts
- **DP over prefixes and block counts**: State `dp[i][t]` tracks the optimal solution using only the first i elements for exactly t blocks.
- **Prefix sums**: Enable O(1) computation of any subarray sum as `pref[r] - pref[l-1]`.
- **Backpointers**: Store decision history to reconstruct the actual subarray boundaries after computing the DP table.
- **Time/space complexity**: Baseline O(n²k) time and O(nk) space; can be optimized with divide-and-conquer or convex hull tricks for larger inputs.

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n + 1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i - 1] + A[i - 1];

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const choice = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => new Array(k + 1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
      choice[i][t] = { type: 'skip', i: i - 1 };

      for (let s = 1; s <= i; s++) {
        const val = dp[s - 1][t - 1] + pref[i] - pref[s - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          choice[i][t] = { type: 'start', s, i };
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct boundaries
  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && i > 0) {
    const c = choice[i][t];
    if (c.type === 'start') {
      blocks.unshift([c.s, c.i]);
      i = c.s - 1;
    } else {
      i = c.i;
    }
    t--;
  }

  return { maxSum: dp[n][k], boundaries: blocks };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests a harder variant of partition DP where each block's value depends on its range (max-min). It requires careful state design, precomputation of subarray values, and backtracking to output exact k non-overlapping blocks.

## Key Concepts
- 2D DP over prefix index and number of blocks
- Precomputing block values V[l][r] = max - min for all subarrays
- Reconstruction via parent pointers to output endpoints

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxRangeSubarrayValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const V = Array.from({ length: n }, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for (let l = 0; l < n; l++) {
    let mx = -Infinity, mn = Infinity;
    for (let r = l; r < n; r++) {
      mx = Math.max(mx, A[r]);
      mn = Math.min(mn, A[r]);
      V[l][r] = mx - mn;
    }
  }

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const parent = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j - 1][t - 1] + V[j - 1][i - 1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = val;
          parent[i][t] = j;
        }
      }
    }
  }

  const blocks = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0 && parent[i][t] !== -1) {
    const j = parent[i][t];
    blocks.push([j, i]);
    i = j - 1;
    t--;
  }
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks: blocks.reverse() };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests a DP over partitioned subarrays with a non-standard per-subarray score and reconstruction.

## Key Concepts
- DP on non-overlapping subarrays
- Prefix sums and range minimums
- Path reconstruction and base cases
- Complexity: O(n^2 k) time, O(nk) space

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxScore(A, k){
  const n = A.length; const P=[0]; for(let i=0;i<n;i++) P[i+1]=P[i]+A[i];
  const dp=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const prev=Array.from({length:n+1},()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++) dp[i][1]=P[i]-Math.min(...A.slice(0,i));
  for(let t=2;t<=k;t++){
    for(let i=t;i<=n;i++){
      for(let p=t-1;p<=i-1;p++){
        const minVal=Math.min(...A.slice(p,i));
        const val=dp[p][t-1]+(P[i]-P[p])-minVal;
        if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t]=val; prev[i][t]=p; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would trace back using prev
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to optimize min queries? N log N via RMQ, or a deque per i.
- How to reconstruct the exact subarrays efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests a non-trivial DP over a linear sequence with a non-crossing constraint and reconstruction of the chosen pairs. It balances readability with the need to optimize across many left endpoints efficiently.

## Key Concepts

- Non-crossing pairings on a line
- DP by right endpoint with reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs; potential 1D optimization for i dimension

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxNonCrossingPairs(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const take = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][0] = 0;
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=k;t++){
      let best = i>0 ? dp[i-1][t] : 0;
      let bestJ = -1;
      for(let j=0;j<i;j++){
        const left = (j>=1) ? dp[j-1][t-1] : (t-1===0 ? 0 : NEG);
        const val = left + Math.abs(A[i]-A[j]);
        if(val > best){ best = val; bestJ = j; }
      }
      dp[i][t] = best;
      take[i][t] = bestJ;
    }
  }
  // reconstruction sketch (omitted for brevity)
  return { value: dp[n-1][k], pairs: [] };
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you enforce exactly k pairs instead of at most k?
- Can you optimize memory to O(n) or derive a monotone queue optimization for certain A distributions?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests minimax-style DP with reconstruction for a classic game.

## Key Concepts
- Two-player DP with difference state
- Subarray DP and reconstruction path
- Time: O(n^2) space: O(n^2)

## Code Example
```javascript
// dp[i][j] denotes max diff for i..j
function maxFirstPlayer(values){
  const n = values.length; const dp = Array.from({length:n},()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  let total = values.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++) dp[i][i]=values[i];
  for(let len=2; len<=n; len++){
    for(let i=0;i+len-1<n;i++){
      const j=i+len-1;
      dp[i][j] = Math.max(values[i]-dp[i+1][j], values[j]-dp[i][j-1]);
    }
  }
  return (total + dp[0][n-1])/2;
}
```

